  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contribution to the UN Development System in Europe and Central Asia and to UNSDCFs in South East Europe</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the 42C/5 1% funds, UNESCO will coordinate and directly contribute to the Regional Collaborative Platform for Europe and Central Asia and related thematic and technical groups (Issue-Based Coalitions, Digital Transformation Groups, Regional Coordination Group on Data and Statistics, Peer Support Group) as well as to the Regional Forum for Sustainable Development (RFSD). In addition, this activity will allow UNESCO to contribute to the roll-out of 4  new UN Sustainable Development Cooperation Frameworks (UNSDCFs) in Bosnia and Herzegovina, North Macedonia, Serbia and T&#xfc;rkiye and to continue implement ongoing UNSDCFs in South East Europe. Moreover, this activity will allow for the strengthening of regional and country strategies in the region covered by the Regional Bureau for Science and Culture in Europe.</narrative>
  </description>
